# ─── EmailJS Configuration (contact form) ──────────────────────────────────
# Sign up at https://dashboard.emailjs.com/ and copy these values into a new
# file called `.env` (this `.env.example` is committed as documentation only).
#
# Once configured, the contact form on the homepage sends emails directly to
# your inbox without any backend. Until you fill these in, the form gracefully
# falls back to opening the visitor's email client via mailto:.

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=

# ─── AI Chatbot (no configuration required) ────────────────────────────────
# The chatbot calls POST /api/chat — a Vercel Serverless Function powered by
# Z.AI GLM (free, no API key) and grounded in src/data/factSheet.js.
# It works out of the box on Vercel. In local dev or any host without the
# function, the bot automatically falls back to the built-in rule-based
# engine (src/utils/chatbotLogic.js), so it never breaks.
#
# Nothing to fill in here — this block is documentation only.
